tps://www.openstreetmap.org/way/42722202"},"additionalOsm":[],"rightsStatus":"review-required","geometryStatus":"draft","attribution":"Open Landmarks; contains © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0","references":[{"title":"File:Église Saint Roch - Paris I (FR75) - 2022-05-27 - 1.jpg","author":"Chabe01","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89glise_Saint_Roch_-_Paris_I_(FR75)_-_2022-05-27_-_1.jpg","sourceSha1":"32cd4c8718719cd645abdb6f7d3bcd5f73759d16","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"exterior"}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["The saved footprint and three roof-part outlines control the plan. OSM contains no heights: nave eave 22 m, ridge 29 m and chapel dome top 30 m are provisional visual inferences, requiring height review.","Cross/apse gables are approximated with the shared mapped gable primitive. The lower outline envelope is inferred at 12 m; no courtyard is filled.","The reviewed Rue Saint-Honoré facade shows paired classical columns and three entrance doors. Six engaged lower columns and dark inset portals now follow the mapped southwest frontage; their spacing is inferred. Sculpture and the upper portal pediment remain simplified."],"source":{"url":"/objects/a81f842172f6b6eca487e17ecffb85b449de5962b99a9a4c8b0ee761b9803ad4/source.blend.gz","bytes":184356,"sha256":"a81f842172f6b6eca487e17ecffb85b449de5962b99a9a4c8b0ee761b9803ad4"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/ebdc52a96cc9155f1